  concept: 'Authored objective: Assemble 124 components and cooling.

    Authored
    requirement: Verify placement, solder contacts and both removable cooling assemblies.

    General
    teaching principle: Thermal control depends on measured temperatures, loads,
    feedback and operating limits over time.

    Only fresh, authoritative game
    evidence can establish that this objective is complete.'
  analogy: A thermostat illustrates the need to distinguish a measured condition
    from a chosen setpoint.
